<pre>-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Debian LTS Advisory DLA-4848-1                debian-lts@lists.debian.org
<a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.debian.org/lts/security/">https://www.debian.org/lts/security/</a>                       Guilhem Moulin
October 21, 2026                              <a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wiki.debian.org/LTS">https://wiki.debian.org/LTS</a>
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Package        : php8.2
Version        : 8.2.35-1~deb12u1
CVE ID         : CVE-2026-109618 CVE-2026-109619

Two critical vulnerabilities were found in PHP, a widely-used open source
general purpose scripting language, which could result in remote
execution of arbitrary code.

CVE-2026-109618

    Out-of-memory handling can interrupt PHP while internal request data
    is only partially initialized.  Request cleanup may then treat the
    invalid data as valid.

CVE-2026-109619

    Request-owned internal global state can survive after its backing
    memory has been freed.  A later request handled by the same worker
    may use that stale state before normal initialization resets it.

For Debian 12 bookworm, these problems have been fixed in version
8.2.35-1~deb12u1.

We recommend that you upgrade your php8.2 packages.

For the detailed security status of php8.2 please refer to
its security tracker page at:
<a  rel="nofollow" href="https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/php8.2">https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/php8.2</a>

Further information about Debian LTS security advisories, how to apply
these updates to your system and frequently asked questions can be
found at: <a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wiki.debian.org/LTS">https://wiki.debian.org/LTS</a>
</pre><p><strong>Attachment:
